## The Challenge

### Breaking the Soda Aisle Stereotype.

The commercial beverage market is polarized. On one side, you have 'Big Soda'—loud, neon, and synonymous with sugar. On the other, you have clinical sparkling waters that feel devoid of personality.

The Alchemist’s Oven faced a unique friction point: How do you take a brand known for the warmth of the oven and translate it into the cool refreshment of a drink? We needed to design a can that didn't look like a cheap sugar rush. It had to signal "Wellness" without looking medicinal, and "Flavor" without looking artificial. The goal was to create a "New Kind of Fizz" —one that a customer would be proud to hold at a dinner party.

